  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "One candle is 12 cm long and takes 4 hours to burn completely. A second candle is 15 cm long and takes 3 hours to burn completely. If both candles are lit at the same time, then find the time taken for the first candle to be twice the height of the second candle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{18}{7}$ hours.",
      "worked": "The burn rates are $12\\div4=3$ cm/hour and $15\\div3=5$ cm/hour. After $t$ hours, the heights are $12-3t$ cm and $15-5t$ cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}12-3t&=2(15-5t)\\\\12-3t&=30-10t\\\\12+7t&=30\\\\7t&=18\\\\t&=\\frac{18}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe first candle is twice the height of the second after $\\dfrac{18}{7}$ hours.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 70
  },
